\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{Counting matrices for induced Gaussian weights}
\date{2026-11-10}

\p{Order the vertices and use the counting basis of the
\vocabk{counting inner products}{fdip-0002}. In that basis the rank-one operator
#{d_e\otimes d_e^\flat} of the
[Gaussian induced action](fdip-005R) has matrix #{d_ed_e^T}, and
#{L_w} has matrix #{-\sum_ew_ed_ed_e^T}. The quadratic energy
#{\langle\phi,Q\phi\rangle} is the coordinate form #{\phi^TQ\phi}.
For the selected split, orthonormal bases of the retained and
eliminated spaces give the block matrix
##{Q=\begin{pmatrix}A&K\\K^*&D_Y\end{pmatrix}.}
The operators themselves do not depend on these bases.}

\p{The determinant expansion in the proof of \ref{fdip-005S} is
this orthonormal matrix calculation. TauCeti's
\leanref/tauceti{Matrix.fderiv_det_apply} states
#{D\det(Q)[A]=\det(Q)\operatorname{tr}(Q^{-1}A)} for a finite
matrix over a complete nontrivially normed field whose determinant
is a unit. Over #{\mathbb R}, positivity supplies that hypothesis.
The declaration supports the determinant derivative. It is not a
theorem about a general noncommutative or infinite-dimensional
determinant. The logarithm, the edge direction and the Gaussian
interpretation are proved in \ref{fdip-005S}.}
